doc Shift-left assignment: x <<= y, short for x = x << y.
  ```
  let n = 3
  n <<= 2
  print n           // 12
  ```

  The left side can be any place of type `int`: a variable, a field, a
  slice element or `*p`, evaluated once.

needs std/let std/addr std/deref std/assign std/shl
syntax statement
  {x: place int} <<= {y: expr int}
expand
  let {$p} = &{x}
  *{$p} = *{$p} << {y}
